                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5583b496-8367-3020-8a94-6f05462437d5",
                        "entry_id": "9fadc42e-9b98-3fa0-b55a-078f38f206cf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een reeks op elkaar volgende denkstappen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "228984dc-ae66-4a2e-bc4e-0e44fdecbc0f",
                                "sense_id": "5583b496-8367-3020-8a94-6f05462437d5",
                                "text": "Het CDA volgt grotendeels dezelfde gedachtegang, al mengt deze partij daar vaak nog het paternalistisch argument doorheen dat het voor migranten zelf ook beter is om weg te blijven: „Wij moeten helaas constateren dat er mensen zijn die het in Nederland niet redden. Dat noemen wij de kansarme migranten. … Wij zien dat de spankracht van de samenleving deze groep op dit moment niet aankan en dat deze mensen en hun kinderen het bovendien zelf ontzettend moeilijk hebben in deze samenleving.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1228b056-4ebb-4a43-872f-cf6bea74ba40",
                                "sense_id": "5583b496-8367-3020-8a94-6f05462437d5",
                                "text": "Wat? Griekse wijn Waar naartoe? Nederland Wijn uit Griekenland? Maken ze daar niet alleen retsina dan? Nee, dat is typisch de gedachtegang van de Nederlandse toerist. Die vliegt naar de goedkoopste bestemmingen op Kreta of Kos. Daar eet hij in de slechtst denkbare tourist trap en komt dus niet in aanraking met de échte Griekse delicatessen. Kortom: Nederlanders hebben geen idee wat er te halen valt in Griekenland. Dit in tegenstelling tot bijvoorbeeld Amerikanen, Fransen of Belgen. Zij tonen in hun reisgedrag meer belangstelling voor cultuur en dus ook voor de traditionele keuken."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9cfd165a-3e9f-46e2-857c-6079fa8db6b9",
                                "sense_id": "5583b496-8367-3020-8a94-6f05462437d5",
                                "text": "Je zegt dat oma Christa om twee redenen boven al dit soort gedachtegangen gestaan zou moeten hebben."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7023e5e1-0bb9-41e1-b535-8fac2e1c7173",
                        "source_entry_id": "9fadc42e-9b98-3fa0-b55a-078f38f206cf",
                        "source_sense_id": "5583b496-8367-3020-8a94-6f05462437d5",
                        "source_sense_description": "een reeks op elkaar volgende denkstappen",
                        "target_lang_word": "Gedankengang",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Gedankengang",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c29dc305-ec11-3d66-a931-189c8e39df64",
                                        "entry_id": "03e6ee90-541f-3446-9e2b-f5ce3c2dfbe1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Abfolge der Gedanken"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33bd4c74-7f56-469e-849f-431d6d76af06",
                                                "sense_id": "c29dc305-ec11-3d66-a931-189c8e39df64",
                                                "text": "Diesen Gedankengang kann ich nicht nachvollziehen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b042f9b-c510-4738-ad57-8eae780b0448",
                                                "sense_id": "c29dc305-ec11-3d66-a931-189c8e39df64",
                                                "text": "„So verliefen die reuigen Gedankengänge des biederen Küan.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "636b163f-5f89-4d09-9cbc-916da13db517",
                                                "sense_id": "c29dc305-ec11-3d66-a931-189c8e39df64",
                                                "text": "„Und dieser so einfache Gedankengang ertötete im Fürsten Andrej alles Interesse, das er früher dem ganzen Reformwerk entgegengebracht hatte.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d1238d0-c3e8-4fde-a252-fdcd566de35f",
                                                "sense_id": "c29dc305-ec11-3d66-a931-189c8e39df64",
                                                "text": "„Dieser kluge Gedankengang stammt übrigens von Epikur, dem wohl ersten Gelehrten, der öffentlich die Existenz Gottes anzweifelte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e7294ae6-92f8-463f-b160-231165df29d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "9fadc42e-9b98-3fa0-b55a-078f38f206cf",
                        "source_sense_id": "5583b496-8367-3020-8a94-6f05462437d5",
                        "source_sense_description": "een reeks op elkaar volgende denkstappen",
                        "target_lang_word": "train of thought",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "train of thought",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ceab2f1a-8feb-3994-b2e1-88c96c98fe90",
                                        "entry_id": "741b8d03-0890-3488-b047-605df3e38c0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The flow of thinking; a sequence of ideas passing through someone’s mind."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8374b0b-1651-4fab-b745-04b3c09d98ca",
                                                "sense_id": "ceab2f1a-8feb-3994-b2e1-88c96c98fe90",
                                                "text": "Did Mr. Winter Wonderland / Say, \"Come 'ere, kid, we really need to talk\"? / Bear with me, man, I lost my train of thought"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36dc11a5-b33d-49d3-9f3e-92bd8c15dcbb",
                        "source_entry_id": "9fadc42e-9b98-3fa0-b55a-078f38f206cf",
                        "source_sense_id": "5583b496-8367-3020-8a94-6f05462437d5",
                        "source_sense_description": "een reeks op elkaar volgende denkstappen",
                        "target_lang_word": "line of thought",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "line of thought",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "13faa010-1d22-3b1d-ab16-97ed1c967f10",
                                        "entry_id": "2f0d7534-f32b-378d-b0bf-be835bee83c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A way of thinking about a particular topic, concept, or problem, that follows a logical progression of reasoning or argument."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "083c6f62-e0db-4271-8c38-8f5972c9dcce",
                                                "sense_id": "13faa010-1d22-3b1d-ab16-97ed1c967f10",
                                                "text": "In the present chapter, I want to develop this line of thought in greater detail and at the same time clear up some difficulties that a number of my critics have claimed to find in my account of these matters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba65571e-009d-4587-81d2-33c0c5391d7b",
                                                "sense_id": "13faa010-1d22-3b1d-ab16-97ed1c967f10",
                                                "text": "Let me approach this line of thought a bit indirectly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa259305-d020-4856-8bea-acab04d6b094",
                                                "sense_id": "13faa010-1d22-3b1d-ab16-97ed1c967f10",
                                                "text": "Similarly, to take twenty-five years of free-form, cross-cutting social, political, economic, and historical writing growing out of work at a single, unstandard, American institution and isolate it as an \"era\" in such writing — a stage, a phase, a line of thought — is to pursue an agenda, take a position, state a case."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e5f2c529-08c6-3162-87a8-1d4a4d4999af",
                                        "entry_id": "2f0d7534-f32b-378d-b0bf-be835bee83c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Way of thinking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d28750c8-b7e6-437d-a936-1a5c4fd6f55a",
                                                "sense_id": "e5f2c529-08c6-3162-87a8-1d4a4d4999af",
                                                "text": "\"Even today there is a dictatorship of a narrow line of thought\" which kills \"people's freedom, their freedom of conscience,\" the Pope expressed in his April 10 daily Mass."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
